questions.question:
What is the theoretical volume of carbon dioxide that can be obtained, at room temperature and pressure, when 1.2 g of Na<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>(s) reacts with 50 cm<sup>3</sup> of 1.0 M HNO<sub>3</sub>?
(Molar volume of gas at room temperature and pressure = 24 dm<sup>3</sup>;
Relative atomic masses: H = 1.0, C = 12.0, N = 14.0, O = 16.0, Na = 23.0)

subQuestions.subQuestion:
Upon completion of the reaction, all the zinc powder was used up. Calculate the theoretical volume of hydrogen gas liberated, measured at room temperature and pressure.
(Molar volume of gas at room temperature and pressure = 24 dm<sup>3</sup>;
Relative atomic mass: Zn = 65.4)

